        "ref": "2CH 16:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the thirty-sixth year of Asa’s reign, Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah, and built Ramah, that he might not allow anyone to go out or come in to Asa king of Judah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2CH 16:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Let there be a treaty between me and you, as there was between my father and your father. Behold, I have sent you silver and gold. Go, break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2CH 16:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Baasha heard of it, he stopped building Ramah, and let his work cease."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2CH 16:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Asa the king took all Judah, and they carried away the stones and timber of Ramah, with which Baasha had built; and he built Geba and Mizpah with them."
      }
